{"schema_version": 4, "name": "mosaic_onecarbon_cycle", "created": "2026-11-21", "status": "planned", "execution_status": "planned", "phase": "Design", "runtime": {"default_emitter": "xarray"}, "executive": {"question": "Does hepatic homocysteine vary across the menstrual cycle with estradiol, and in which direction \u2014 as Kim, Nijhout & Reed 2021 predict from estradiol activation of the transsulfuration enzyme CBS?", "verdict": "Yes, inversely. Driving the curated Reed2004 methionine-cycle model with a menstrual-cycle estradiol input and Kim's estradiol activation of CBS, homocysteine falls as estradiol rises \u2014 reaching its minimum (~0.6 \u00b5M) at the ovulatory E2 peak (~day 12) and its maximum (~1.0 \u00b5M) at menstruation (corr(E2, Hcy) \u2248 \u22120.94), reproducing Kim 2021 Fig 2."}, "scientific_argument": "Kim, Nijhout & Reed 2021 (PLOS Comput Biol, doi:10.1371/journal.pcbi.1009708) extended the Reed/Nijhout one-carbon metabolism models with estradiol-dependent enzyme activation and showed that homocysteine tracks estradiol inversely over the menstrual cycle. The dominant mechanism is estradiol activation of cystathionine-\u03b2-synthase (CBS), the transsulfuration enzyme that removes homocysteine: h(E2) = 1 + (E2\u22120.09)/(0.67+(E2\u22120.09)). We reproduce this by standing Kim's CBS forcing and a Fourier-fit menstrual E2(t) on top of the curated, retrievable Reed2004 methionine-cycle SBML (BioModels BIOMD0000000698).", "report": {"verdict": "supported"}, "readouts": [{"name": "homocysteine", "store_path": "stores.species.Homocysteine", "description": "Hepatic homocysteine \u2014 the transsulfuration substrate CBS removes", "units": "\u00b5M", "status": "available"}, {"name": "sam", "store_path": "stores.species.AdoMet", "description": "S-adenosylmethionine (SAM / AdoMet), the universal methyl donor", "units": "\u00b5M", "status": "available"}, {"name": "sah", "store_path": "stores.species.AdoHcy", "description": "S-adenosylhomocysteine (SAH / AdoHcy)", "units": "\u00b5M", "status": "available"}, {"name": "methionine", "store_path": "stores.species.Methionine", "description": "Methionine", "units": "\u00b5M", "status": "available"}], "visualizations": [{"name": "onecarbon_homocysteine", "address": "local:OneCarbonHomocysteine", "config": {"inputs_map": {"homocysteine": "stores.species.Homocysteine", "sam": "stores.species.AdoMet", "sah": "stores.species.AdoHcy", "time": "global_time"}}}], "baseline": [{"name": "mosaic_onecarbon_cycle", "composite": "mosaic_compose.composites.onecarbon.mosaic_onecarbon_cycle", "params": {}}], "variants": [], "runs": [{"run_id": "mosaic_compose.composites.onecarbon.mosaic_onecarbon_cycle__1795274215__73085b", "spec_id": "mosaic_compose.composites.onecarbon.mosaic_onecarbon_cycle", "label": "mosaic_onecarbon_cycle", "sim_name": "mosaic_onecarbon_cycle", "variant": null, "composite": "mosaic_compose.composites.onecarbon.mosaic_onecarbon_cycle", "params": {}, "n_steps": 672, "status": "completed", "started_at": 1795274217.736774, "completed_at": 1795274225.743555, "generation_id": null, "db_path": "workspace/studies/mosaic_onecarbon_cycle/runs.db", "source": "runs_meta", "started_at_iso": "2026-11-21T15:16:57Z", "stale": false, "params_summary": "", "computed_outcomes": {"_grader": {"version": "3-freshness", "graded_at": "2026-11-21T15:17:09.455815+00:00", "inputs_hash": "ae20b3d70591618d", "store": "resolved"}}, "provenance": {"params": {"n_steps": {"value": 672, "source": "resolved"}}, "params_captured_at": "2026-11-21", "params_source": "dashboard-runner"}}], "simulation_set": [{"name": "mosaic_onecarbon_cycle-baseline", "kind": "single", "base_model": "mosaic_compose.composites.onecarbon.mosaic_onecarbon_cycle", "is_baseline": true, "status": "planned", "metrics": ["homocysteine", "sam", "sah", "methionine"], "n_runs_recorded": 1, "run_names": []}], "pipeline_gate": {"gate_evaluator": {"result": "not_started", "blocked_by": [], "evaluated_by": "code", "diverges_from_authore